{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/140251-spirit-claimed-pc","id":140251,"title":"Spirit claimed pc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-16T22:06:07-07:00","id":140251,"title":"Spirit claimed pc","content":"I have talked with my st and brought up the idea of playing a spirit claimed. he finds the idea interesting and may let me do it at a future time (current character is a demon...kinda how i stumbled on but unrelated). I first found it in Book of spirits but think i will pull it more from Wtf: predators because it is more fleshed out there.<br /> <br /> <u>Only a few questions will i pose but are quite major and they are as follows:</u><br /> <br /> 1) would snipping out the attribute bonuses cripple the character too much?(a suggestion of mine to not power game)<br /> 2) could a spirit grow after it has claimed a host?(still capable of consuming essence after all)<br /> 2b) if so how would you suggest?<br /> <br /> ....cant think of any other questions at the moment. I just find the concept cool and a great potential way to have a story contributing character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T01:06:14-07:00","id":140324,"title":"","content":"Hm not sure on the growth aspect. As for stat bonuses, if you're going for realism I'd only go with what the spirit would actually go for. There's several write ups of spirit claimed that you can research to see what you like. The Forsaken demo, Manitou Springs, features quite a few. I think predators also has shapeshifters as spirit claimed as well. <br /> <br /> The evolutionary standpoints... eh... I dunno. Maybe? If you're able to increase your spirit rank in some way you could learn new Numina? Not entirely sure how they work in that regard. I usually just think about killing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T03:11:54-07:00","id":140380,"title":"","content":"Perhaps take a look at the purified from immortals, and mash that with the playable rules for revenants in mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:25:41-07:00","id":140611,"title":"","content":"I'll take a look at the suggested wrighting.<br /> <br /> main reason I'm curious about rank increase isn't attribute or numai bonuses by 'synthesis' the bonus the claimed get, so a way for character to still grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachme